{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_9","type":"agent_message","text":"**NOT READY.** Three rules can still change the verdict for the same set of answers.\n\n1. **Part B needs exact source boundaries.** For `6955`, `e3956` says NVIDIA confirmed a definitive agreement on September 3. It does not establish that the agreement was signed on September 2, as the target specifies. The SEC filing `e3768` does. For `591`, `e41` and `e120` support the 2028 delay but omit the PCB cause. Decide which details are required before scoring. Also give wrong attribution precedence over unsupported when an answer uses a wrong source and has no correct one. [Kyber target](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-21-citation-lists/probe-targets.json:30) · [Agreement target](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-21-citation-lists/probe-targets.json:59) · [Reading rules](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-21-citation-lists/PROBE-DESIGN.md:86)\n\n2. **Part C must count repeated loss by claim.** In `control-1:8790`, one control can support the $393B reference with `e195` and another with `e669`. If all three v12 answers lose that reference, rule (a) still misses it because neither source was used twice. Count the two controls as supporting the same claim. Give readers the quotes for shared sources too, as §3 requires. The packet in §4 currently specifies only sources that differ. [Part C harm rule](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-21-citation-lists/PROBE-DESIGN.md:104) · [Reading packets](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-21-citation-lists/PROBE-DESIGN.md:145)\n\n3. **Give the outcome code one verdict for overlapping cases.** A run with an unresolved material Part C difference can satisfy every listed pass condition and also qualify as inconclusive. An A1 format rejection also leaves a missing answer, while skipping optional A2 must leave the core verdict alone. Specify which outcome takes precedence and rehearse those cases. [Outcome and rehearsal](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-21-citation-lists/PROBE-DESIGN.md:123)"}}
